1
00:00:01,329 --> 00:00:07,694
(Q1) MARTHA: Hi Alex. It's Martha Clines here. James White gave me your number.&nbsp;

2
00:00:07,694 --> 00:00:10,186
I hope you don't mind me calling you.

3
00:00:10,186 --> 00:00:12,030
ALEX: Of course not. ALEX：

4
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:13,245
How are you, Martha?

5
00:00:13,245 --> 00:00:15,010
MARTHA: Good thanks. MARTHA：

6
00:00:15,010 --> 00:00:18,988
I'm ringing because I need a bit of advice.

7
00:00:18,988 --> 00:00:20,924
ALEX: Oh yeah. ALEX：What about?

8
00:00:20,924 --> 00:00:25,015
MARTHA: The training you did at JPNW a few years ago. MARTHA：

9
00:00:25,015 --> 00:00:27,574
I'm applying for the same thing.

10
00:00:27,574 --> 00:00:29,603
ALEX: Oh right. ALEX：

11
00:00:29,603 --> 00:00:31,584
[Example] Yes, I did mine in 2014.

12
00:00:31,584 --> 00:00:33,228
Best thing I ever did.

13
00:00:33,228 --> 00:00:34,475
I'm still working there.

14
00:00:34,475 --> 00:00:35,929
MARTHA: Really? MARTHA：

15
00:00:35,929 --> 00:00:37,807
What are you doing?

16
00:00:37,807 --> 00:00:44,282
[Q1答案句 + Q1干扰项] ALEX: Well, now I work in the customer services department but I did my initial training in Finance.&nbsp;

17
00:00:44,282 --> 00:00:48,611
I stayed there for the first two years and then moved to where I am now.

18
00:00:48,611 --> 00:00:52,326
(Q2) MARTHA: That's the same department I'm applying for.&nbsp;

19
00:00:52,326 --> 00:00:53,528
Did you enjoy it?

20
00:00:53,528 --> 00:00:57,076
ALEX: I was pretty nervous to begin with.&nbsp;

21
00:00:57,076 --> 00:01:01,407
[Q2答案句： math /Math / Mathematics] I didn't do well in my exams at school and I was really worried because I failed Maths.

22
00:01:01,407 --> 00:01:05,543
But it didn't actually matter because I did lots of courses on the job.

23
00:01:05,543 --> 00:01:13,329
(Q3) [Q3答案句] MARTHA: Did you get a diploma at the end of your trainee period?&nbsp; I'm hoping to do the one in business skills.

24
00:01:13,329 --> 00:01:14,965
ALEX: Yes. That sounds good.

25
00:01:14,965 --> 00:01:19,265
[代词指代， 答案已经说过了] I took the one on IT skills but I wish I'd done that one instead.

26
00:01:19,265 --> 00:01:21,756
MARTHA: OK, that's good to know.&nbsp;

27
00:01:21,756 --> 00:01:24,736
(Q4) What about the other trainees?

28
00:01:24,736 --> 00:01:27,318
How did you get on with them?

29
00:01:27,318 --> 00:01:38,249
[Q4答案句+Q4干扰项] ALEX: There were about 20 of us who started at the same time and we were all around the same age - I was 18 and there was only one person younger than me, who was 17. ALEX：

30
00:01:38,249 --> 00:01:41,168
The rest were between 18 and 20.

31
00:01:41,168 --> 00:01:43,006
I made some good friends.

32
00:01:43,006 --> 00:01:47,484
(Q5) MARTHA: I've heard lots of good things about the training at JPNW. MARTHA：

33
00:01:47,484 --> 00:01:51,206
It seems like there are a lot of opportunities there.

34
00:01:51,206 --> 00:01:53,204
ALEX: Yeah, definitely. ALEX：

35
00:01:53,204 --> 00:01:58,084
Because of its size you can work in loads of different areas within the organisation.

36
00:01:58,084 --> 00:02:04,801
[Q5干扰项] MARTHA: What about pay? I know you get a lower minimum wage than regular employees.

37
00:02:04,801 --> 00:02:10,338
[Q5答案句] ALEX: That's right - which isn't great.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;But you get the same number of days' holiday as everyone else.

38
00:02:10,338 --> 00:02:15,261
And the pay goes up massively if they offer you a job at the end of the training period.

39
00:02:15,261 --> 00:02:22,043
(Q6) MARTHA: Yeah, but I'm not doing it for the money - it's the experience I think will be really useful.&nbsp;

40
00:02:22,043 --> 00:02:26,425
[跟定位词] Everyone says by the end of the year you gain so much confidence.

41
00:02:26,425 --> 00:02:27,897
ALEX: You're right.&nbsp;

42
00:02:27,897 --> 00:02:29,894
That's the most useful part about it.

43
00:02:29,894 --> 00:02:32,398
There's a lot of variety too.

44
00:02:32,398 --> 00:02:34,672
You're given lots of different things to do.

45
00:02:34,672 --> 00:02:38,557
I enjoyed it all - I didn't even mind the studying.

46
00:02:38,557 --> 00:02:43,913
[Q6答案句，一方提出，另一方表态 = 代词指代] MARTHA: Do you have to spend any time in college?&nbsp;&nbsp;ALEX: Yes, one day each month.&nbsp;

47
00:02:43,913 --> 00:02:47,765
So you get lots of support from both your tutor and your manager.

48
00:02:47,765 --> 00:02:53,283
(Q7) [company出现] MARTHA: That's good.&nbsp; And the company is easy to get to, isn't it?

49
00:02:53,283 --> 00:02:59,390
[Q7答案句： location 。  ... is a real advantage = ... is convenient] ALEX: Yes, it's very close to the train station so the location's a real advantage.&nbsp;

50
00:02:59,390 --> 00:03:02,321
(Q8) ALEX: Have you got a date for your interview yet? ALEX：

51
00:03:02,321 --> 00:03:06,157
MARTHA: Yes, it's on the 23rd of this month. MARTHA：

52
00:03:06,157 --> 00:03:09,996
ALEX: So long as you're well prepared there's nothing to worry about. ALEX：

53
00:03:09,996 --> 00:03:11,670
Everyone's very friendly.

54
00:03:11,670 --> 00:03:17,242
[Q8跟定位： wear] MARTHA: I am not sure what I should wear. What do you think?

55
00:03:17,242 --> 00:03:21,094
[Q8答案句， 否定 = nothing too ... , like ... = don't wear] ALEX: Nothing too casual - like jeans, for example.&nbsp;

56
00:03:21,094 --> 00:03:25,559
If you've got a nice jacket, wear that with a skirt or trousers.

57
00:03:25,559 --> 00:03:26,801
MARTHA: OK. MARTHA：

58
00:03:26,801 --> 00:03:27,525
Thanks.

59
00:03:27,525 --> 00:03:30,051
(Q9) Any other tips?

60
00:03:30,051 --> 00:03:34,819
ALEX: Erm, well I know it's really obvious but arrive in plenty of time.&nbsp;

61
00:03:34,819 --> 00:03:36,771
[Q9答案句： hate people who are ... = don't be ...] They hate people who are late.

62
00:03:36,771 --> 00:03:40,440
So make sure you know exactly where you have to get to.

63
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:47,267
(Q10) [Q10答案句] And one other useful piece of advice my manager told me before I had the interview for this job - is to smile.

64
00:03:47,267 --> 00:03:49,427
Even if you feel terrified.

65
00:03:49,427 --> 00:03:51,777
It makes people respond better to you.

66
00:03:51,777 --> 00:03:56,387
MARTHA: I'll have to practise doing that in the mirror!&nbsp;

67
00:03:56,387 --> 00:03:58,822
ALEX: Yeah - well, good luck.&nbsp;

68
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:01,340
Let me know if you need any more information.

69
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:03,840
MARTHA: Thanks very much.

